Short:        ZX Spectrum emulator for MorphOS
Author:       Michal Zukowski
Type:         misc/emu
Version:      1.9.2
Architecture: ppc-morphos
Requires:     MorphOS >= 3.18
Distribution: Aminet

Fuse 1.9.2 for MorphOS
======================

Fuse is a ZX Spectrum emulator with support for many Spectrum models,
peripherals and common tape, disk and snapshot formats.

This MorphOS version provides a native MUI interface and MorphOS video,
audio, input and requester support.

Requirements
------------

  - MorphOS 3.18 or newer

Installation
------------

Unpack Fuse.lha to any directory and keep the supplied directory structure
intact. Everything required to start the MorphOS port is included in the Fuse
directory.

Start the emulator by double-clicking the Fuse icon/executable from Ambient,
or run Fuse from Shell.

Do not move the roms, lib, ui or Catalogs directories away from the Fuse
program directory.

Video
-----

The MorphOS port provides three video modes:

  Surface
    Software rendering. The window size follows the selected Fuse scaler or
    filter.

  Overlay
    Hardware-assisted CGXVideo output when available. The window can be
    resized and the image keeps its aspect ratio.

  TinyGL
    TinyGL accelerated output when available. The window can be resized and
    the image keeps its aspect ratio.

If an accelerated video mode cannot be opened, Fuse falls back to another
available mode.

Fullscreen uses a dedicated MorphOS screen. Overlay and TinyGL use the Ambient
screen mode and scale the picture to the largest possible size while keeping
the correct aspect ratio. Surface fullscreen chooses a screen size suitable
for the active scaler or filter.

Localization
------------

English text is built into the program. A Polish catalog is included in:

  Catalogs/polski/Fuse.catalog

MorphOS Locale preferences select the language automatically.

The Catalogs directory also contains translation source files for people who
want to prepare additional languages.

Preferences
-----------

Fuse can be configured from its MUI menus. An example MorphOS preferences file
is supplied as:

  Fuse_MorphOS_prefs.example

MorphOS-specific preferences may be stored as:

  ENV:Fuse_MorphOS_prefs
  ENVARC:Fuse_MorphOS_prefs

The example file documents the available MorphOS-specific options.

Included files
--------------

The distribution contains the Fuse executable together with the ROMs, UI
data, font and locale files needed by this MorphOS port. Keep these files in
their original directories below the Fuse program directory.

